  "details": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated users to delete other users' AI voice records by supplying an arbitrary userId to DELETE /airag/voice/deleteVoiceRecord. Attackers can obtain record ids from the unchecked GET /airag/voice/listByUser endpoint and delete victims' text-to-speech history entries stored in Redis, one per request.",
